C029,Better Connectivity Plan for Regional and Rural Australia,Commitment,Action Plan,"Department of Infrastructure, Transport, Regional Development, Communications and the Arts",Commonwealth Government,x,,x,,,The Government has committed to a Plan with significant funding to improve rural and regional telecommunications.,"Resourcing: The Plan provides for major upgrades of the National Broadband Network (NBN) and funding for rural and regional telecommunications infrastructure, including multi carrier mobile expansion ($400 million), local connectivity ($200 million), farm-based solutions ($30 million), national mobile coverage audit ($20 million) and further funding for Regional Tech Hub ($6 million).  The $160 million combined grant opportunity for Regional Connectivity Program Round 3 and Mobile Black Spot Program Round 3 opened on 20 March 2023, Applications are due by 12 July 2023. (see RCP and MBSP item above) Indigenous Specific: No Responsible Minister/s: Minister for Communications Delivery Timeframe: 2022-27 (funding under the Plan is available over five years)",National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,,,,,,,,x,
