C040,Cultural Capability Matters: Queensland Government Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Cultural Capability Training Strategy,Commitment,Strategy,"Department of Treaty, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Partnerships, Communities and the Arts",State Government,,x,,Also see the Queensland Government Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Cultural Capability Framework. All Queensland Government agencies have their own Cultural Capability Action Plans.,,,,State,Queensland,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,x,,,,,
C041,Cultural Safety in Health Care for Indigenous Australians Monitoring Framework,Commitment,Framework,Department of Health and Aged Care,Commonwealth Government,x,,,,,"The Department of Health and Aged Care commissioned the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare (AIHW) to develop and maintain the Cultural Safety in Health Care for Indigenous Australians Monitoring Framework, which provides yearly updates on relevant cultural safety data for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people in the Australian health system. The AIHW has published annual data on cultural safety measures in health care for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people since October 2019. The web report for this framework was updated on 29 June 2022.","Resourcing: The AIHW has been commissioned for a total of $752,773 from 2017-18 to 2024-25 to develop and maintain the framework Indigenous Specific: Yes Responsible Minister/s: Minister for Health and Aged Care Delivery Timeframe: 2017-18 to 2024-25",National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,,x,,,,
