C050,Disability Sector Strengthening Plan,Commitment,Action Plan,All signatories to the National Agreement,Other,x,x,x,"Jurisdictional annual Closing the Gap reporting, and their review by Joint Council, are the key accountability mechanisms for monitoring and reporting on implementation of the Sector Strengthening Plan.",,"Develop Disability and First Nations engagement principles and protocols to prioritise the voices of First Nations people with disability, their families and communities in policy, service delivery and practice (Disability Sector Strengthening Plan)",Resourcing: Costs are to be absorbed within existing resources Indigenous Specific: Yes Responsible Minister/s: Minister for Social Services Delivery Timeframe: 2022-2025,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,x,,,,,x,,,,
C051,Early Childhood Care and Development Sector Strengthening Plan (Partnership Action),Commitment,Action Plan,Department of Education (Commonwealth),Commonwealth Government,x,x,x,"Jurisdictional annual Closing the Gap reporting, and their review by Joint Council, are the key accountability mechanisms for monitoring and reporting on implementation of the Sector Strengthening Plan.",,"The three-year Early Childhood Care and Development Sector Strengthening Plan (ECCD-SSP) outlines transformative sector strengthening actions to support and build the First Nations community controlled early childhood care and development services sector, with the key areas for action being:
C052,Early Years Strategy,Commitment,Strategy,Department of Social Services,Commonwealth Government,x,,,,,"The Government has committed to develop and implement a whole-of-Commonwealth. Early Years Strategy (Strategy) to create a new integrated and holistic approach to investments in the early years. The Strategy will be developed over the next 12 months. Key activities include establishing governance arrangements, undertaking stakeholder consultation, mapping existing Commonwealth programs and funding and developing policy priorities. The Early Childhood Care and Development Policy Partnership will also inform the development of the Strategy. The Strategy will also build on and complement existing Closing the Gap measures including the National Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Early Childhood Strategy, the National Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Early Childhood Strategy, Education Council and Early Childhood Care and Development Sector Strengthening Plan.",Resourcing: $4.2 million over 18 months from June 2022 Indigenous Specific: No Responsible Minister/s: Minister for Social Services | Minister for Youth Delivery Timeframe: 2024,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,,,x,,,,,,
C053,Ending Rheumatic Heart Disease: Queensland First Nations Strategy 2021-2024,Commitment,Strategy,Queensland Health,State Government,,,,"Partnered Regional Action Plans sit under this. See also the Queensland First Nations Rheumatic Heart Disease Alliance, the Queensland Rheumatic Heart Disease Register and Control Program, and the Regional Health System Dashboard.",,,Includes action plan,State,Queensland,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,x,,x,,,x,,,,
