N017,First Deputies Group,Network,Forum,Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet,Commonwealth Government,,x,,,"Comprised of first deputies from equivalent Departments of Premier and Cabinet in all states and territories. Regularly discusses cross-jurisdictional matters, including the implementation of the National Agreement and the broader First Nations policy agenda.",FDG supports First Secretaries Group to progress policy issues and other taskings from the National Cabinet.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,,,,,,
N018,First Nations Action Board (FNAB),Network,Board,"Department of Youth Justice, Employment, Small Business and Training",State Government,,,,,Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Youth Justice staff members from across Queensland. They work in a range of positions from front line staff to managers. Every member is a strong advocate and leader within Youth Justice and their local communities.,To help Youth Justice develop culturally appropriate ways to reduce over-representation of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people in the youth justice system.,,State,Queensland,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,x,,,x,,,
N019,First Nations Advisory Council,Network,Advisory Body,National Disability Insurance Agency,Commonwealth Government,,,,,Commonwealth Government,"To work with NDIA and First Peoples Disability Network to discuss and make shared decisions about the goals, strategies and initiatives that affect First Nations people with disability.",,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,,,x,,,,
N020,First Nations Clean Energy Steering Committee,Network,Network,First Nations Clean Energy Network,Aboriginal Community-Controlled Organisation,,,,,"Cultural leaders who are specialists from the clean energy industry, law, investment, academia, unions, business and community sectors. ",Guides the operation of the First Nations Clean Energy Network to ensure that First Nations communities  share in the benefits of the clean energy boom.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,x,,,,x,,x,,,x
N021,First Nations Consultative Committee (FNCC),Network,Committee,"Department of Treaty, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Partnerships, Communities and the Arts",State Government,,,,,"Members of the Committee are: Mr Terry O’Shane (Co-chair), Far North Queensland region; Ms Talei Elu (Co-chair), Torres Strait region; Ms Karen Dini-Paul, Cape York Peninsula region; Mrs Patricia Lees, Gulf and West Queensland region; Mr Edward Smallwood, North Queensland region; Mr Joshua Gorringe, Central Queensland region; Ms Kerry Crumblin, South West Queensland region; Mr Cameron Costello, South East Queensland region.","Established in 2022 for 12 months to develop an Indigenous Voice preferred model for Queensland. Represents First Nations communities in eight regions – Cape York Peninsula, Far North Queensland, Gulf and West Queensland, North Queensland, Central Queensland, South West Queensland, South East Queensland, and the Torres Strait.",The FNCC will report back to the Qld Govt by the end of 2023. ,State,Queensland,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,x,x,,,,,,,,
N023,First Nations Referendum Working Group,Network,Working Group,National Indigenous Australians Agency,Commonwealth Government,,,,,"Minister for Indigenous Australians, the Hon Linda Burney MP and Special Envoy for Reconciliation and the Implementation of the Uluru Statement from the Heart, Senator Patrick Dodson, co-chair the First Nations Referendum Working Group. The Attorney-General, the Hon Mark Dreyfus KC MP works alongside the Minister and Special Envoy to support the work of the Referendum Working Group. It is made up of diverse First Nations leaders from across Australia who have had longstanding involvement in the process for constitutional recognition.",To advise the Government on the referendum. Its focus includes: the timing of the referendum; the wording of the constitutional amendment and question; information about the principles of the Voice.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,,,,,,
N024,First Nations Youth Advisory Group,Network,Advisory Body,Office for Youth,Commonwealth Government,,,x,Part of the Youth Engagement Model CTG implementation measure,One young person representing each state and territory,To provide advice to the NIAA on the development of the Early Years Education Capacity and Innovation Fund,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,x,,,,,,
N025,First Secretaries Group,Network,Forum,Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet,Commonwealth Government,,x,x,,Chaired by the Secretary of the Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet and comprising Secretaries and Directors-General from state and territory First Ministers’ departments.,The FSG facilitates engagement between the Commonwealth and states and territories and considers policy issues and provides advice prior to discussion by First Ministers at National Cabinet. The National Cabinet tasks the First Secretaries with critical policy work.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,,,,,,
N026,Health Chief Executices Forum,Network,Forum,Department of Health and Aged Care,Commonwealth Government,,,x,,Health department chief executive officer from each state and territory and the Australian Government.,Forum for joint decision-making and strategic policy discussions that helps to efficiently deliver health services in Australia.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,,,,,x,,,,
