N031,International Decade of Indigenous Languages Directions Group,Network,Steering Committee,"Department of Infrastructure, Transport, Regional Development, Communications and the Arts",Commonwealth Government,,,,Oversees Voices of Country - Australia's Action Plan for the International Decade of Indigenous Languages 2022 - 2032,"18 members: 13 Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander members, including two members representing First Languages Australia; and five ex-officio members from key Government agencies (the Department of Infrastructure, Transport, Regional Development, Communications and the Arts, Australian Institute of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Studies, the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, the National Indigenous Australians Agency and the Department of Education).",To shape Australia's participation in the UNESCO International Decade of Indigenous Languages 2022–2032 (the International Decade).,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,,,,,,,,,x
N032,Joint Coordinating Committee (JCC),Network,Committee,"Department of Treaty, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Partnerships, Communities and the Arts",State Government,,x,x,,"LGAQ, Queensland Government, community representatives. Details here.","To provide oversight of the co-design and implementation of the Local Thriving Communities (LTC) reform, which will bring greater decision-making authority to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities across the state.",,State,Queensland,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,,,,,,,
N033,Joint Council on Closing the Gap,Network,Working Group,Closing the Gap,Commonwealth Government,,x,x,,"Indigenous Affairs Ministers, Coalition of Peaks, ALGA","To support national leadership, coordination and cooperation on Closing the Gap and provide advice to the Council of Australian Governments (COAG) as appropriate. The Joint Council will finalise the refreshed Closing the Gap framework and targets and review the 2008 National Indigenous Reform Agreement. The Joint Council will have an ongoing role in monitoring performance against the jointly agreed framework and targets. The Joint Council will also monitor implementation, noting jurisdictions will determine how they implement the Closing the Gap agenda in a manner that is consistent with the overarching national framework. All COAG Councils are required to progress Indigenous Affairs matters as part of their normal business. This Joint Council will work in cooperation with other COAG Councils on an asneeds basis.",,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x
N035,Leaders in Indigenous Nursing and Midwifery Education Network (LINMEN),Network,Network,Department of Health and Aged Care,Commonwealth Government,Y,,,,Unknown,"To (i) support nursing and midwifery educators to provide the highest quality education and training on cultural safety and First Nations health, history and culture (ii) contribute to graduating nurses and midwives who are better prepared to provide culturally safe health services to First Nations people and (iii) support the recruitment and retention of First Nations nurses and midwives.",Resourcing: $2.51 million (ex GST) from 2022-23 to 2025-26 Indigenous Specific: Yes Responsible Minister/s: Minister for Health and Aged Care Delivery Timeframe: Completion due by 30 June 2026,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,x,,x,,,,
N036,Local Community Engagement through Co-Design (LCETC) Project Board,Network,Board,Department of Education (Queensland),State Government,,,,,"Representatives from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities, Commonwealth government representatives from the National Indigenous Australian Agency (NIAA), Department of Seniors, Disability Services and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Partnerships representatives and Department of Education (DoE) staff.","To improve outcomes for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students in Queensland state schools.The LCETC model is a strategic approach to assist schools to establish, maintain and leverage relationships with the local Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander community to co-design programs of work that will assist Indigenous students to succeed at school.",,State,Queensland,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,x,,,,,,
N037,Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Data Governance Forum,Network,Forum,Australian Institute of Health and Welfare,Commonwealth Government,,,,See also the National Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Agreement ,"Commonwealth, state and territory health representatives and key stakeholders including peak bodies, key organisations and lived experience representatives.  The current membership of the MHSPDGF consist of standing members, which are parties to the National Agreement, or where representation is specified in the National Agreement: Co-Chair, Australian Government Department of Health and Aged Care; Co-Chair, NSW (nominated by state and territory health departments); State and territory health department representatives; Australian Government Department of Health and Aged Care; Primary Health Network representatives; A mental health consumer representative; A mental health carer representative; A representative with lived experience of suicide; A First Nations lived experience representative; A First Nations data representative. The MHSPDGF also includes appointed observers, which are agencies with the expertise necessary to progress the work the MHSPDGF oversees. Appointed observers: Australian Institute of Health and Welfare; National Mental Health Commission; National Suicide Prevention Office; Australian Bureau of Statistics; Mental Health Australia; Suicide Prevention Australia."," To oversee and facilitate the implementation of the data and performance measurement commitments specified in the National Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Agreement (the National Agreement). The scope of the MHSPDGF is to agree on authorising frameworks and systems for data sharing and linking, improve national consistency in data collections, agree on appropriate measurement and monitoring methodologies to support evaluation of services and the mental health system and to provide technical advice on other relevant data and outcome activities.",,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,,x,,,x,,,,
N038,Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Senior Officials Group (MHSPSO),Network,Advisory Body,Department of Health and Aged Care,Commonwealth Government,,,,See also the National Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Agreement ,Includes representatives from each jurisdiction. Four lived or living experience members.,Established to progress implementation of the National Agreement. Reports to Health Chief Executives and Health Ministers. Supported by Working Groups and Project Groups established as needed.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,,,x,,,,
N039,National Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health Protection AHPPC Sub-Committee (NATSIHP),Network,Committee,Department of Health and Aged Care,Commonwealth Government,x,,,Sub-committee of the Australian Health Protection Principal Committee (AHPPC),The NATSIHP co-chair are the National Aboriginal Community Controlled Health Organisation (NACCHO) and the Department of Health and Aged Care. Full list of members at https://www.health.gov.au/committees-and-groups/the-national-aboriginal-and-torres-strait-islander-health-protection-ahppc-sub-committee#members,"NATSIHP provides holistic and culturally safe advice on health protection matters for First Nations peoples and communities. NATSIHP’s focus is on communicable and chronic diseases, environmental health, and disaster management in primary health settings, and health issues related to COVID-19. NATSIHP is the first AHPPC sub-committee to exclusively focus on First Nations peoples and communities.  ",Resourcing: Costs are to be absorbed within existing resources Indigenous Specific: Yes Responsible Minister/s: Minister for Health and Aged Care Delivery Timeframe: Ongoing with the group meeting fortnightly. NATSIHP's first official meeting was held on 26 October 2022.,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,x,,,,,x,,,,
N041,National Cabinet,Network,Other,Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet,Commonwealth Government,,x,,,Chaired by the Prime Minister and comprises all state premiers and territory chief ministers. A representative of Local Government is invited to meet with National Cabinet once each year.,"Collaborate on matters of national significance and importance according to agreed priority areas, which include early learning and child development, workforce participation, and health system reform.",Formerly known as the Council of Australian Governments (COAG),National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,,,,,,
N042,National Federation Reform Council,Network,Advisory Body,Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet,Commonwealth Government,,x,,,"National Cabinet, the CFFR and the Australian Local Government Association (ALGA)",To focus on priority national federation issues.,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,x,,,,,,,,
N043,National Workforce Plan Project Reference Group,Network,Reference Group,Department of Health and Aged Care,Commonwealth Government,,x,x,Developed the National Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health Workforce Strategic Framework and Implementation Plan 2021 - 2031,The National Health Leadership Forum (NHLF); the National Aboriginal Community Controlled Health Organisation (NACCHO); Lowitja Institute; Gayaa Dhuwi (Proud Spirit) Australia; Australian Indigenous Doctors’ Association (AIDA); National Association of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander; Health Workers and Practitioners (NAATSIHWP); representatives from state and territory governments; the Australian Government.,,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,,,,,,,x,,,,
N044,Partnership Priorities Committee,Network,Committee,Department of Social Services,Commonwealth Government,,,,A sub-committee of the Secretaries Board,"The Secretary of the Department of Social Services (Co-chair); The CEO of the National Indigenous Australians Agency (Co-chair); The Secretary of the Department of Education; The Secretary of the Attorney-General’s Department; The Secretary of the Department of Employment and Workplace Relations; The Secretary of the Department of Infrastructure, Transport, Regional Development, Communications and the Arts; The Australian Public Service Commissioner; The Secretary of the Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water; The Secretary of the Department of Industry, Science and Resources","To steer better policy and delivery outcomes for Australians. We do this by further embedding partnership culture and behaviour in the public service. We want to ensure a consistent, natural and early impulse to engage and co-design with: First Nations People; communities; states and territories; business; unions; non-government organisations (NGOs); tertiary sector.",,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,,,,,,,,,,
N045,Partnership Working Group,Network,Working Group,Coalition of Peaks; Joint Council on Closing the Gap,Commonwealth Governement; State Government; Aboriginal Community-Controlled Organisation,,,x,Also known as the Drafting Group. A function of the Joint Council on Closing the Gap.,Indigenous Affairs Officials from all governments and Coalition of Peaks,Supports the Joint Council on Closing the Gap. The Partnership Working Group develops and progresses issues for upcoming Joint Council meetings,,National,N/A,N/A,N/A,N/A,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x,x
