S053,Headspace (Youth mental health),Stakeholder,NGO,N/A,NGO,Y,N/A,,,,"As part of the 2021-22 Budget, funding was provided to improve access to culturally safe mental health services for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander young people through the headspace network $8.7 million over three years to the Western NSW Primary Health Networks for headspace outreach services; $5.6 million over four years to the Northern Territory Primary Health Network for headspace outreach services and to establish headspace Palmerston - Ongoing funding of approximately $1.0 million per annum for the headspace Pilbara project. As part of the 2022-23 Budget, $1.3 million over four years from 2022-23 was provided to the Country SA Primary Health Network (PHN) to continue the Flying headspace program.","Resourcing: $8.7 million from 2021-22 to 2023-24, $5.6 million from 2021-22 to 2024-25, 
